@startuml JesusCrust_vs_Brimstone
scale 1.25
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "App JS / UI" as App

package "JesusCrust boundary" {
  rectangle "JS host adapter\n(main-thread DOM commit gate + telemetry)" as Host
  rectangle "Rust core / WASM worker\n(store · selectors · scheduler · patch generator)" as RustCore
  rectangle "JS execution harness\n(currently QuickJS-backed transactional tests)" as Harness
}

package "Brimstone engine subsystems" {
  rectangle "Parser & bytecode builder" as Parser
  rectangle "Bytecode VM + interpreter" as VM
  rectangle "Runtime & intrinsics" as Runtime
  rectangle "Compacting GC & heap" as GC
}

App --> Host : batched patch intent, input events
Host --> RustCore : delta streams, scheduling hints
RustCore --> Host : deterministic patch batches
Host ..> Harness : optional regression path
Parser --> VM : emits bytecode
VM --> Runtime : invokes intrinsics + objects
Runtime --> GC : allocates, scavenges
Harness ..> Parser : future research path only

note left of RustCore
  Non-borrowable zone: scheduler/graph/patch format remains bespoke to JesusCrust’s reactivity surface.
  Host adapter + telemetry surface stays minimal and JC-owned.
end note

note right of Harness
  Current state: JC harness is independent.
  Future research only: Brimstone may inform semantics probes or tooling.
  Borrowed test/fuzz patterns extend this harness or run beside it.
end note

note right of GC
  Brimstone is a standalone JS engine; DOM access remains gated by JesusCrust’s host.
end note

@enduml
